# Engram + OpenSpec (RHCL)

Engram MCP is available (project binding is **per-developer** via local `.engram/config.json`, gitignored). Use it proactively — the user must not need to ask.

Canonical SDD store: sibling `../migration-toolkit-sdd/` (OpenSpec). Product `AGENTS.md`: do not use Engram for new SDD artifacts — use OpenSpec.

## Authority

| Knowledge | Authoritative store | Engram |
|-----------|---------------------|--------|
| Change specs, tasks, design | SDD `openspec/changes/` … `openspec/specs/` | Never substitute |
| **Design / architecture decisions** | SDD **`design.md`** | **Also `mem_save` (dual-write)** |
| Workflow gotchas, CI, preferences | Engram | Primary |

Full policy: `../migration-toolkit-sdd/.cursor/rules/engram.mdc` and `docs/sdd-backlog.md`.

## Dual-write for design / architecture

1. Update SDD `design.md` (OpenSpec change) first.
2. Then `mem_save` (`type`: architecture/decision, `topic_key`: `rhcl/architecture/<slug>`, link to OpenSpec path in content).

SDD wins on conflict; Engram is for cross-session recall and context injection.

## Proactive use

Save after significant work; search at session start on related topics; `mem_session_summary` before closing substantial sessions.
